---
/**
 * /privacy — R11, Pass B. THIS BRIEF IS THE SPEC; CONTEXT.md carries no
 * entry for this round. See the Pass B prompt for the ruling behind
 * every decision below.
 *
 * NOT A HUB SECTION. No id in src/data/sections.ts, no folio entry, no
 * masthead, no place in the ten-<h2> structure. One document in one
 * column, Porcelain throughout — no Cover, no pivot, no photograph, no
 * Obsidian ground. Chrome is FOOTER ONLY: Masthead and FolioMarginalia
 * are neither imported nor touched, and this file adds no entry to
 * sections.ts, because every one of the masthead's and the folio's
 * anchors resolves against the hub's own sections and every one of them
 * is dead here.
 *
 * COPY IS SET VERBATIM FROM PRIVACY.md, including the standfirst's
 * literal date, which lives in the source rather than as a token the
 * build substitutes. Nothing is reworded, added, or cut. Section order
 * is PRIVACY.md's order.
 *
 * THE STANDFIRST IS THE PAGE'S ONLY WAY BACK. Footer-only chrome is a
 * dead end otherwise. PRIVACY.md's standfirst already names her — "Dr.
 * Syreeta McClain. Last updated September 16 2026." — so the fix is to link the
 * name that is already there, not to invent a navigation device. Set in
 * the masthead name's own register (Fraunces, opsz 24 / wght 400 /
 * SOFT 60 / WONK 0) at the coda tier's size (Pass B.1), with a resting
 * underline from PageFooter's link treatment and .mast-home's own
 * interaction, copied rather than imported: opacity 0.7 on hover, 0.55
 * on active, 260ms, opacity only, and R16's own focus ring (1px solid
 * Obsidian, 4px offset). Masthead.astro is not
 * opened for this — its <style> is component-scoped and importing the
 * component would mount the whole bar, which this route must not carry.
 *
 * THE MEASURE IS CAPPED AT max-width: 39.4118em, PASS A's VALUE,
 * BYTE-FOR-BYTE. .win-body (the page's own generic body window) gives
 * up to nine columns in band 1, which is far past a comfortable
 * measure at 1920 with no cap — exactly the defect Pass A fixed in
 * About. The em is written on .privacy-body, which also carries
 * font-size: var(--bio-size), so it resolves against the same 17px
 * context Pass A measured against (670px), not against some ancestor's
 * font-size. THIS SWEEP IS NOT RE-RUN — the ruling says confirm it
 * holds for this copy and STOP AND REPORT if it does not; see the Pass
 * B report for the per-paragraph, per-width table.
 *
 * NO grid-column IS HAND-SET. .win-body is the one primitive this file
 * needs — a single column of text with no live margin — reused exactly
 * as it already exists in global.css rather than adding a page-specific
 * one. h1, the standfirst, the opening statement, and each section
 * entry are its only children, seated in the same window every hub
 * section's body copy already uses.
 *
 * ONE <h1>, "Privacy Policy". Then one <h2> per PRIVACY.md section, in
 * its order. This is a different document from the hub's ten spreads
 * and takes its own heading structure; nothing here is added to satisfy
 * the hub's locked structure, because that structure does not apply to
 * this route.
 *
 * ZERO JAVASCRIPT ON THIS ROUTE. No island, no script, no listener.
 * BaseLayout's inline `js-motion` switch and the grain sheet are shared
 * page infrastructure mounted on every route already; nothing new is
 * added here, and this file imports no island and adds no client
 * directive, so it contributes no new JS chunk and no new
 * <astro-island>.
 *
 * GOLD: ZERO. The one rule per section entry is Smoked Slate at 0.38,
 * the same hairline every other section on the site draws — CONTEXT.md
 * routes every new rule to Slate; the saturated-accent budget (3 of 3)
 * is untouched because nothing here is gold at all.
 *
 * OUT OF SCOPE, NOT TOUCHED: Masthead.astro, FolioMarginalia.astro,
 * sections.ts, PageFooter.astro, every hub component, COPY.md,
 * PRIVACY.md, CONTEXT.md. PageFooter is mounted exactly as it ships on
 * the hub, including its hardcoded `on-obsidian` ground and its
 * self-referential Privacy Policy link on this page — both reported in
 * the Pass B report, neither fixed here, per the brief's instruction
 * that a shared component's regression risk is not worth this page's
 * fix.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageFooter from '../components/PageFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — Dr. Syreeta McClain">
  <main>
    <section class="sheet privacy">
      <h1 class="win-body privacy-h1">Privacy Policy</h1>

      <p class="win-body privacy-standfirst">
        <a class="privacy-home" href="/">Dr. Syreeta McClain</a>. Last updated September 16 2026.
      </p>

      <p class="win-body privacy-lede">This site collects almost nothing. Here is exactly what it does collect, where it goes, and what you can ask us to do about it.</p>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">What this site is</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>drsyreetamcclain.com is a set of static pages. There are no accounts to create, nothing to buy, no advertising, no analytics, and no tracking cookies. You can read every page on this site without giving us anything at all.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Do Not Track</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>Some browsers send a Do&nbsp;Not&nbsp;Track signal, and some send a Global&nbsp;Privacy&nbsp;Control signal, asking a site not to follow you from one website to the next. This site does not follow you anywhere, and no advertiser or analytics service watches you here, so there is nothing for those signals to switch off. We honor them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">What you can give us</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>The only place this site accepts information is the contact form. It asks for four things: your name, your email address, the type of inquiry you are making, and your message. That is the whole list. We do not ask for anything else and we do not collect anything else from you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Where an inquiry goes</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>When you send the form, it is handled by Formspree, a form processing service, which delivers it to us by email. Inquiries about the Everyday&nbsp;Legends&nbsp;Foundation go through the <a href="/#sec-contact">contact form</a> to the Foundation, because it is a separate organization. Every other inquiry goes through the <a href="/#sec-contact">contact form</a> to Dr.&nbsp;McClain.</p>
          <p>We use what you send us to answer you. That is all. We do not sell it, we do not share it for advertising, and we will not add you to a mailing list.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Spam protection</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>The contact form uses Cloudflare&nbsp;Turnstile to tell a person from a bot. There is no puzzle to solve. Your browser sends Cloudflare technical signals about the request so it can make that judgment. Cloudflare's own privacy policy governs what it does with them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Hosting</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>The site is hosted by Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel records standard technical information about requests, including IP address, browser type, the page requested, and the time. This keeps the site running and secure. We do not use it to build a profile of you.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">How long we keep inquiries</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>We keep messages for as long as we need them to respond and to keep a reasonable record of the conversation. If you would like your message deleted, write to us and we will delete it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">How your message is held</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>This site keeps no database and has no accounts, so nothing you send is stored on the site itself. Your message lives in the same protected mailboxes as the rest of our correspondence, and only the people who need to answer you read it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Your choices</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>You can ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. Write to us through the <a href="/#sec-contact">contact form</a> and we will take care of it. Some information may need to be kept where the law requires it.</p>
          <p>If you live somewhere with specific privacy laws, including the European Union and California, those laws may give you additional rights. We honor them where they apply.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Children</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <!-- The sentence a district reader looks for. PRIVACY.md marks it
               bold in source; <strong> carries that emphasis into the
               render. font-weight is stated explicitly below because body
               sets font-synthesis-weight: none — a bare <strong> at the UA
               default (bolder / 700) has no loaded weight to render and no
               synthesis to fall back on, so it would sit at the browser's
               nearest match and look identical to the paragraph around it.
               500 is the heaviest Montserrat weight this page loads. -->
          <p>This site is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from them. <strong>No student information is collected through this site</strong>, and nothing here is connected to any school or district system. If you believe a child has sent us information, write to us and we will delete it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Links to other sites</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>This site links out to premierleadersllc.com, everydaylegend.com, the district website, and the McClain brothers' sites. Those are separate sites with their own privacy practices. Read theirs before sharing anything with them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Changes</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>If this policy changes, we post the new version on this page and change the date at the top. There is no mailing list here, so this page is the notice. Check the date to see whether anything has moved since you last read it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="win-body privacy-entry">
        <hr class="privacy-rule" />
        <h2 class="privacy-h2">Contact</h2>
        <div class="privacy-body">
          <p>Questions about this policy, or about information you have sent us? Write to us through the <a href="/#sec-contact">contact form</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <PageFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Standalone route, standard rhythm — the same value About and Contact
     both carry. Not one of the ten hub sections, so the Composition
     table's "sections MUST NOT share a padding token" does not bind
     here; reusing 96 is a choice of restraint, not a collision. */
  .privacy{
    padding-block: 96px;
  }

  /* ---- H1 ----------------------------------------------------------
     --fx-display, the page's own prominent-heading token (Cover's name,
     the blog's kicker head), stated with its own weight the same way
     every other consumer of this token does — Fraunces defaults to
     wght 900 if a rule leaves it unstated. */
  .privacy-h1{
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-display);
    font-weight: 340;
    font-size: clamp(40px, 4.2vw, 58px);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* ---- STANDFIRST ----------------------------------------------------
     PASS B.1: the masthead name's register (opsz 24 / wght 400 / SOFT 60
     / WONK 0, -0.01em) at the CODA TIER's size, clamp(26px, 2.2vw, 32px)
     — About's and Educational Leader's closing line.

     NOT --mast-name-size. That token is --lede-size x (--lede-size /
     --quote-size); below 1280 the pivot's clamp floors and the ratio
     rises past 1, so the name grew as the viewport shrank — 61.45px
     against a 52px lede at 390. The coda tier covers the masthead name's
     own band-1 range (26-32 against 26.66-32), holds still below 1280,
     and sits between the lede (>=52) and the body (17) at every width. */
  .privacy-standfirst{
    margin: var(--s2) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24, 'wght' 400, 'SOFT' 60, 'WONK' 0;
    font-size: clamp(26px, 2.2vw, 32px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-wrap: pretty;              /* No orphans */
  }

  /* .mast-home's interaction, copied rather than imported, PLUS a resting
     underline — hover opacity alone left the link undiscoverable in
     running text. The underline is PageFooter's .foot-privacy treatment
     (1px, 4px offset); its colour there is --rule-ui, which exists only
     under .on-obsidian, so this takes that treatment's own light-ground
     value, Slate at 0.42 (.edu-link, .mast-jump). Opacity only. */
  .privacy-home,
  .privacy-body a{
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(71, 68, 64, 0.42);
    transition: opacity 260ms var(--ease);
  }
  .privacy-home:hover,
  .privacy-body a:hover{ opacity: 0.7; }
  .privacy-home:active,
  .privacy-body a:active{ opacity: 0.55; }
  .privacy-home:focus-visible,
  .privacy-body a:focus-visible{
    outline: 1px solid var(--obsidian);
    outline-offset: 4px;
  }

  /* ---- OPENING STATEMENT ---------------------------------------------
     The page's lede tier, verbatim — --fx-lede, the same face, axes,
     weight, clamp, line-height and letterfit every section's opening
     statement already carries. Display type, so the measure ceiling
     this file states below does not apply to it, the same exemption
     About's own lede carries. */
  .privacy-lede{
    margin: var(--s5) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: var(--fx-lede);
    font-weight: 350;
    font-size: var(--lede-size);    /* was the token's clamp restated; reads the token so the lede cap reaches it */
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.018em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  /* One rhythm value between every section entry, including the first —
     margin-top only, so gaps never stack across a grid formatting
     context (grid items do not collapse adjoining margins the way block
     boxes do). */
  .privacy-entry{
    margin: var(--s6) 0 0;
  }

  /* The hairline head, Educational Leader's and Contact's own idiom:
     rule, then heading. Smoked Slate at 0.38 — the same weight every
     hairline on the site uses. NOT GOLD: CONTEXT.md routes every new
     rule to Slate: "the budget is spent. Add none." */
  .privacy-rule{
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s2);
    border: 0;
    background: var(--slate);
    opacity: 0.38;
  }

  /* ---- H2 ------------------------------------------------------------
     A third tier, between the lede and the body — the same coordinates
     About's and Educational Leader's coda already carry (opsz 96 /
     SOFT 35 / wght 400), reused rather than re-derived because this
     page's headings are exactly that register: display type, clearly
     subordinate to an opening statement, clearly senior to body copy. */
  .privacy-h2{
    margin: 0 0 var(--s3);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96, 'wght' 400, 'SOFT' 35, 'WONK' 0;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2vw, 30px);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--obsidian);
  }

  /* ---- BODY, AND THE MEASURE CAP --------------------------------------
     --bio-size / --bio-lh, the page's body tokens, unchanged — and
     max-width: 39.4118em on the SAME rule that sets font-size, so the
     em resolves against this element's own 17px, not an ancestor's.
     That is what makes it Pass A's exact 670px rather than a
     coincidentally similar number in a different font context. */
  .privacy-body{
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-weight: 300;
    font-size: var(--bio-size);
    line-height: var(--bio-lh);
    letter-spacing: 0.004em;
    color: var(--slate);
    text-wrap: pretty;
    orphans: 3;
    widows: 3;
    max-width: 39.4118em;
  }

  .privacy-body strong{
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .privacy-body p{ margin: 0; }
  .privacy-body p + p{ margin-top: 1.5em; }
</style>
